A||||2||sid1200||88 GT suspension noise/squeaks||||1||
Z||000000||sid1200||05-08-2000||03:45 AM||||have had this problem for a while, but its now gotten worse.  the car basically has a constant squeak/groan noise coming from the both the front and rear of the car, more on the front I think.  This is pretty constant when traveling over pretty much any road irregularities but worse over bumps esp at low speeds.  Sometimes esp when the car is cold it doesn't do this at first.  <P>I've replaced the shocks/struts and the car has 27k on it.  I've heard the best way is to replace the bushings, but not sure which ones, I've been told, just the stabilizer bar ones, and others told me all of them.  Also I'm trying to stay away from Poly bushings since I live in San Francisco, and don't want a rough ride, factory ride/handling is a good compromise for me at this point.  So question is , are the factory rubber bushings available new, and from whom?  and what should I do/replace to solve this.  The car is otherwise perfect and this has just become embarrasing with all the squeaks.  thanks a bunch||||reg||1
Z||000001||lawrence||05-08-2000||01:02 PM||||I had a squeak in the rear of my 88 GT.  I got some silicone brake fluid and put a couple drops on all the bushings.  That stopped the squeak.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine<p>[This message has been edited by lawrence (edited 05-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||05-08-2000||04:54 PM|||| Factory bushings usually don’t make noise like that except for the sway bar bushings. Polyurethane bushings will make all kind of noises if they are not greased. Maybe your car has polyurethane bushings on it. If you bought it used this could be possible.||||reg||1
